            <h2 id="interpretation" class="band">Interpretation</h2>
            <p>&ldquo;We&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, &ldquo;our&rdquo; and &ldquo;the house&rdquo; refer to the owners of Corner House, Braunston, and the property let. &ldquo;You&rdquo;, &ldquo;your&rdquo; and &ldquo;guests&rdquo; refer to the person making the booking and everyone staying at the house. These terms, together with our booking rules, house rules and refund policy, make up the agreement between us.</p>

            <h2 id="the-agreement" class="band">The agreement</h2>
            <p>These terms form a legally binding agreement after your booking has been confirmed in writing. Your booking is made on the basis of the information and photographs on this website, and the description in the rental agreement. We have taken reasonable care to ensure these are accurate, but do not rely on them as statements of fact and we reserve the right to make reasonable changes where necessary.</p>

            <h2 id="pricing" class="band">Pricing</h2>
            <p>Prices are for the whole house, per night, for up to 12 adults and 2 children. The nightly rate varies by season (low, shoulder and high), and a cleaning fee applies to every booking. A refundable security deposit is collected with the balance. We may occasionally offer promotional prices at our discretion. Prices shown are estimates; the total due is confirmed when your booking is confirmed.</p>

            <h2 id="payment" class="band">Payment</h2>
            <p>A non-refundable deposit of 25% of the total is required to secure your dates, with the balance due 8 weeks before arrival. Bookings made within 8 weeks of arrival are payable in full at the time of booking. We may require additional payment if you add guests or services after booking. Payment is due on the date agreed; if we do not receive it, we may treat the booking as cancelled.</p>

            <h2 id="security" class="band">Security deposit</h2>
            <p>A refundable security deposit is collected with the balance. It is held against damage, breakages and any additional cleaning or loss caused by the party. We will return it within 7 days of your departure, less any reasonable deductions, which we will itemise. Damage should be reported as soon as it happens so we can do our best to repair it.</p>

            <h2 id="your-stay" class="band">During your stay</h2>
            <p>You are responsible for your party and agree to comply with the house rules, and to leave the house, its furniture and its grounds in the same condition as you found them. If anything is broken or damaged, please tell us promptly. You agree to allow access for reasonable maintenance, with notice where possible. We may terminate your booking without refund if you or your party behave in a way that is unreasonable, dangerous, or in breach of these terms or the house rules.</p>

            <h2 id="direct" class="band">Staying direct</h2>
            <p>Direct bookings are 10% cheaper than the platform rate. They require a signed rental agreement, photo ID from the lead guest, and payment as set out above. Direct bookings must comply with these terms. Booking through a platform is subject to that platform&rsquo;s own terms and cancellation policy instead.</p>

            <h2 id="cancellation" class="band">Cancellation</h2>
            <p>If you cancel, the refund you receive depends on when you cancel and is set out in our <a href="#refunds">refund policy</a>. If we have to cancel your booking (for example, through damage or circumstances beyond our control), we will refund all money you have paid and will not be liable for any further costs you incur. Nothing in these terms limits either party&rsquo;s rights under the law.</p>

